---
orbit 2026
component AnnouncementBar
settings {
  text: Text = "Free shipping on orders over 2,000" label "Message"
  link: Text = "" label "Link URL"
  tone: Select("neutral", "accent", "dark") = "accent" label "Tone"
}
---
{# PORT NOTE (announcement-bar): clean.

   The original computes `background: s.background` from a colour setting. Here
   `tone` is a closed set of three, so the colour lives in the stylesheet and
   the template picks a class. That is a BETTER design than the original — the
   merchant cannot pick an unreadable colour pair — but it is a narrowing, and
   it is only available because the set is small enough to enumerate. See the
   colour finding in the report. #}
<div class="ann ann--{settings.tone}">
  <if {settings.link != ""}><a class="ann__link" href={settings.link}>{settings.text}</a></if>
  <else><span>{settings.text}</span></else>
</div>
